<speak>A steady pace is best, thanks. I've deliberately cleared the afternoon because I'm trying to stop squeezing personal matters between business calls. The family business can fill every available space if I let it. My daughter asked why I can arrange meetings for everyone else but never arrange an afternoon with her. That was a bit of a wake-up call. So I've started reserving some time at home, even if it's only to have lunch together without a phone on the table.</speak>